Z||000006||contra||08-17-2000||06:48 PM||||Visceral, i bought the air dam from fiero shop here in toronto canada for around $110 canadian. it was easy to put on, and i just fiberglassed it onto the original fascia to retain that stock look. i think i did a fairly decent job.<BR>the damn itself was pretty flimsy because it needed to flex to the shape of the fascia, so i rienforced it with some fiberglass and believe it or not, spray insulation foam. it's hard as a rock now  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||DXR_DAD||08-17-2000||08:46 PM||||Man Contra that is one SWEET GT!!!!!!!! I love that front end air dam!!!!<P>I know Monkeyman wants one?? now I do too!<BR>I can tell from the pics that you take very good care of you ride....Good Keep up the good work.  ("Rodent Killer Air Dam") <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>DXR_DAD||||reg||11
Z||000008||zeusrekning||08-17-2000||09:26 PM||||contra,<BR>That is sharp!!!<BR>I, also 18, know what it is like trying to get into the car hobby. I'm lost most of the time and bad about taking advise from any one. I have had quite a few cars.<BR>ford festiva  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">    (wrecked)<BR>87 mitsubitchi pickup (screwed up suspension lowering)<BR>71 lemans (wrecked)<BR>geo metro (messed up)<BR>87 fiero (drive now)<BR>77 firebird (building now)<P>any ways great job <BR>And remember we have got to take the position of all these old guys in the future.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||14
Z||000009||Sillhouette.com||08-17-2000||10:26 PM||||Great looking car and paintjob.  A couple of suggestions if you will.  Must be nice that where you live front licence plates are not required by law.  You are right about the rims aftermarket ones will look much better.  Get a spacer for the rear rims just enough to have the top of the tire almost in line with the fender.  Lower the car that will give it a mean stance not to mention great handling.  Loose the wing.  The fastback looks so much cleaner without it.  It's also unique.  A lot of Fieros have those wings on it.  I only know of three that don't.  You'd be the fourth.  <P>Later (I wish I had a car like this at 18)||||reg||1
Z||000010||contra||08-17-2000||10:40 PM||||naw i have to have the plate in the front too, it's just i'm letting the paint harden alot more before i go screwing that fiero licence plate holder onto the front...i dont want any premature scratches. I might paint the holder the same colour as my car too, i'm not sure yet.  I'm going to be looking for rims for the next while, i have to build up my bank account for the next little while though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>Also, i think i'll keep my fiero spoiler tho, i like the wing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
Z||000011||Sillhouette.com||08-17-2000||10:45 PM||||Another suggestion that I've forgott to mention.  Get one of those clear plastic chip protectors and stick it to the front of your car before you get paint chips.  <P>Later||||reg||1
